---

Drain the @chick peas{1 tin}(425 g), keeping the liquid. Put the chick peas in a food processor with the @garlic{1%clove}(peeled) and whizz to a thick purée, scraping down the sides as necessary. Add the @light tahini{2%tbsp}, @olive oil{5%tbsp}, a tablespoonful of the @lemon juice{2%tbsp} and a little of the reserved chick pea liquid, and whizz again. Keep on adding the reserved liquid until a smooth creamy consistency, like lightly whipped cream, is obtained. Taste the mixture and add more lemon juice if necessary then season with @salt and @pepper.

To serve, spoon the hummus into a bowl, swirl a little olive oil on top and sprinkle with @paprika.